{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s48-p01",
      "text": "Would you be able to sleep with one eye open?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p02",
      "text": "Bottlenose dolphins can.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p03",
      "text": "When they sleep, only half of their brain goes to sleep.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p04",
      "text": "They sleep with one eye open to stay safe.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p05",
      "text": "Half of their brain sleeps for about two hours before the other half gets a chance to sleep.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p06",
      "text": "Dolphins are not fish—they are mammals.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p07",
      "text": "The smallest dolphin is about 50 kilos heavy, while the largest kind of dolphin weighs up to 10 tons.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p08",
      "text": "These mammals have lungs.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p09",
      "text": "They have to go to the surface of the water to get fresh air.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p10",
      "text": "These energetic animals can be seen near the coast, sometimes swimming alongside boats.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p11",
      "text": "Dolphins don't lay eggs.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p12",
      "text": "Their young are born alive, and they drink milk from their mothers.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p13",
      "text": "Dolphins are smart and brave.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p14",
      "text": "Some dolphins save people from shark attacks.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p15",
      "text": "They are able to solve many problems and even use tools to catch fish.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p16",
      "text": "But their cleverness doesn't end there.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p17",
      "text": "Dolphins can also pass on anything they learn to other dolphins.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p17.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p18",
      "text": "They show great teamwork.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p18.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p19",
      "text": "They communicate with each other using sounds like whistles and clicks.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p19.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p19.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p20",
      "text": "Maybe they make sentences just as humans do!",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p20.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p20.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p21",
      "text": "Dolphins know the \"voices\" of other dolphins and even know exactly from whom the sounds are.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p21.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p21.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p22",
      "text": "They can also know themselves in a mirror and check different parts of their bodies in it.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p22.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p22.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p23",
      "text": "However, dolphins have been facing danger from humans.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p23.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p23.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p24",
      "text": "There are people shooting them with their guns, causing wounds that make them bleed to death.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p24.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p24.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s48-p25",
      "text": "We should protect the smart animal for a better future, not only for theirs, but also for ours.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p25.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s48-p25.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
